# Test-Driven Development

**`main` (mod) policy.** Base-game branch `master` has no unit-test suite. All new mod work on `main` requires TDD for production behavior.

## Iron Law

No production behavior without a failing test first. If implementation landed before the test, delete it and start over.

## Red → Green → Refactor

1. **RED** — One minimal test for one behavior. `@DisplayName` + AssertJ (`Assertions.assertThat`).
2. **Verify RED** — Fails for missing behavior, not a typo/setup error.
3. **GREEN** — Smallest change that passes.
4. **Verify GREEN** — Re-run; all must pass.
5. **REFACTOR** — Clean up only after green; no new behavior.

```bash
./gradlew :core:test --tests "com.shatteredpixel.shatteredpixeldungeon.heroechoes.EchoAndStorageTest"
./gradlew :core:test --tests "com.shatteredpixel.shatteredpixeldungeon.heroechoes.EchoAndStorageTest.fromHeroCapturesRequiredFields"
```

## Test quality

- One behavior per test; split if the name needs "and".
- Prefer **real fixtures** over mocking the game (`GdxTestExtension`, `EchoTestSupport`). Test seams (`set…ForTests`) are fine.
- Mirror production packages under `core/src/test/java/`.
- Never fix a bug without a failing reproduction test first.
- EchoBoss / world-VFX combat: use skill `echo-combat-vfx-test` / `EchoTestSupport.installEchoBossLevel` — hollow sprite-less fights hide NPEs.

## Good vs Bad

```java
// ✅ GOOD
@Test
@DisplayName("rejects snapshot when depth is invalid")
void rejectsInvalidDepth() {
	Assertions.assertThatThrownBy(() -> Echo.create(-1, ...))
		.isInstanceOf(IllegalArgumentException.class);
}

// ❌ BAD — vague, asserts almost nothing
@Test
void testSnapshot() {
	Assertions.assertThat(Echo.create(5, ...)).isNotNull();
}
```

## Done checklist

- [ ] Behavior had a failing test first
- [ ] Minimal green; `./gradlew :core:test` clean
- [ ] Feature work: report **tests created**, **gaps**, **redundant** (`@DisplayName` titles); ask before filling/removing

## Exceptions (ask if unsure)

Throwaway prototypes, generated code, config-only (rules/AGENTS/ignore), assets, i18n `.properties`, version/changelog bumps, pure renames with existing coverage.
